# Cloudflare Pages headers config.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# T082 — sprint v3 rewrite.
#
# Problem this file used to have:
#   The catch-all `/*` block's `Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate`
#   was CONCATENATED onto the more-specific `/_next/static/*` immutable
#   rule, producing the broken header
#       Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable, no-store, must-revalidate
#   on every hashed chunk. Browsers honored the no-store half and refetched
#   every asset on every page load — disastrous LCP.
#
#   Cloudflare's _headers spec says more-specific rules SHOULD win, but the
#   live deployment proved otherwise. The only safe fix is to remove the
#   `/*` catch-all and enumerate every HTML route explicitly.
#
# Strategy:
#   1. Hashed static bundles → immutable, cache forever.
#   2. API routes → no cache (always hit the function).
#   3. Every HTML route gets its own block with cache + security headers.
#      Security headers are duplicated rather than inherited from a /*
#      catch-all (because CF concatenates).
#   4. Favicon → short revalidate so a brand-mark refresh propagates in
#      a day, not a month.
#
# Adding a new top-level HTML route? Copy the /sign-in block and rename
# the path. Forgetting to add a route means no security headers ship —
# add a test or grep before deploy.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Static asset bundles — immutable, content-hashed filenames
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/__next-on-pages-dist__/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/icon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# V4-fix — SW kill switch. /sw.js MUST NOT cache (browsers check for SW
# updates on every navigation, plus we want the kill-switch contents to
# replace any stale registration ASAP). Content-Type is critical so the
# browser actually treats this as a service worker.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Content-Type: application/javascript
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /

/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API routes — never cache. CSP not applied (JSON responses).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HTML routes — enumerated. Each gets:
#   - Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate (T082.1)
#   - HSTS, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy,
#     Permissions-Policy, Content-Security-Policy (T082.2)
#
# CSP notes:
#   - unsafe-inline + unsafe-eval needed today for Next.js inlined client
#     bundles + the build-time runtime preamble. Tighten with nonces in a
#     follow-up sprint (see DECISIONS.md D-014).
#   - connect-src allows *.supabase.co + wss://*.supabase.co for the
#     Supabase JS client (HTTPS REST + realtime WebSocket).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

